I visited all 3 altars :-( I thought death was gonna be... you know...
like, deadly tough :-) I guess I over-rated him. Rodney visited
several
times, but I gave him the /oDeath each time.

But geeze, the end-game riders were easy. Perhaps it was my role...
and these babies:

 b - the blessed fireproof +0 Longbow of Diana (weapon in hand)
 t - 14 blessed rustproof +6 arrows named storm
 C - 42 blessed poisoned rustproof +6 arrows named storm (in quiver)

With 200+ more in my BoH. It took sometimes only 2 turns to kill an
Angel. The first time I saw death, it only took 1 turn to kill.

Nonetheless, I owe my victory to r.g.r.nethack, and a ton of luck.
I started with 3 magic lamps, found 5 Magic Markers randomly
throughout the dungeon. Heck, I ascended with 3 wishes left :-)

Lessons learned:

* GET THE EYE IF YOU CAN. The Eye of the Aetheopica is probably
the best thing that happened to me this game, and was well worth
a wish. Magicbane was... nice. With Liches genocided, there was
no big issue with curses.

* Alchemy... was awesome. Getting a hundred extra HP for
endgame is just... great.

* Conflict was great. Damn, that was a good ring. Opponents were
too busy fighting each other than fighting me. It allowed me to just
walk through crowds... course, the -48 AC probably helped too :-)

* Endgame riders are some trash... at least... when dealt with afar.
I don't know what would happen if I engadged them in melee combat,
but I don't want to find out.

* Rodney sometimes takes 2 or more /oDeath to kill. Bounce
them off the wall to have a higher chance of killing him. But make
sure you have reflection.

Wow... I've finally won. I finally have beaten Nethack... Again,
thanks
for all your help guys.

